      "reviewer": "Codex primary implementer",
      "decision": "The public selectedOptions model is constructed with multiplicity and replaced before content initialization with the existing selected identities when multiplicity changes. Option _setSelected calls select/deselect on that same model; ngAfterContentInit observes changed.added/removed and synchronizes option state under takeUntil(_destroyed). The component-owned compareWith resolves values to concrete options in _setOptionsFromValues rather than supplying a model comparator. The exposed model can be operated on by consumers: genuine original/minimum public executions verify initial identities, event.source/add/remove arrays and no-op suppression, cached sort order, deferred clears and observer unsubscription. The genuine original comparator setSelection defect is reproduced and both minima fix it; the separately prepared packed legacy exposure case has not run and its upstream SHA remains pending. Current change return declarations narrow boolean-or-void to boolean without widening accepted arguments. Cyph has no direct selectedOptions/SelectionModel/compareWith references in the recorded authored source scan. Stable nondeprecated public declarations are proven; no product HTML/CSS/SCSS or TypeScript change is necessary for this dependency boundary. This does not qualify actual list option synchronization, forms, browser rendering or full supported floors.",
