      "decision": "The runtime public SelectionModel import is constructed with the existing multiple boolean and default identity/event settings. The owned _selectOptionByValue resolves custom compareWith values, skips already-selected option identities and handles null/comparator errors before selecting concrete options. clear/select/deselect/isSelected/isEmpty and sort use only documented nondeprecated public members; changed.added/removed drives option selection under takeUntil(_destroy). The two inherited first-selected reads in select.ts are separately source-bound. Whole authenticated original/current minimum modules preserve exact selection/change arrays, membership, cached sort ordering, deferred clear and unsubscription. Strict generic consumers exercise public types with four rejecting type controls; current boolean change results narrow the original boolean-or-void result and owned calls do not depend on it. No private comparator implementation or new bulk API is imported or used. Cyph uses the legacy selectors and styles recorded by the read-only sanity check without direct model/comparator API use. No consumer API/HTML/CSS/SCSS change is required for this boundary; complete packed select interaction, layout, destruction and runtime/RxJS floors remain separate gates.",
